    "created_at": "2022-06-15T00:05:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-15T00:05:36Z",
    "body": "\"unsalvageable\" is the spec language for eviction. An inactive document that is still salvageable can still be navigated to.\r\n\r\nBroadcastChannel prevents < 0.1% of BFCache usage, so it's low priority for chrome to improve.\r\n\r\nSo, the question is whether we should spec that receiving a broadcast message evicts. What is the bad thing that would happen some impl decided to just queue the messages and deliver them on restore?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1155823325/reactions",
