    "updated_at": "2022-06-15T02:27:01Z",
    "body": "> \"unsalvageable\" is the spec language for eviction. An inactive document that is still salvageable can still be navigated to.\r\n\r\nThis isn't accurate. Salvageability is used for [determining whether a document can stay in bfache at unload time](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#unload-a-document). Eviction consists of [nulling out a session history entry's document at some later time](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-session-history-of-browsing-contexts:discard-a-document-2) and is unrelated to salvageability.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1155911138/reactions",
